  "prompt": "A small picture is stored as a grid: an array of rows, each row an array of whole numbers. Turning the picture a quarter turn **clockwise** moves its left column to the top row, read upwards from the bottom. For example, turning\n\n```\n1 2 3\n4 5 6\n```\n\nclockwise gives\n\n```\n4 1\n5 2\n6 3\n```\n\nWrite `rotateRight(grid)` that takes a grid with 0 to 5 rows, where every row has the same length (1 to 5 numbers), and returns the rotated grid as a new array of arrays. A grid with no rows returns `[]`. The input must not be changed.\n\nExamples:\n\n- `rotateRight([[1,2,3],[4,5,6]])` returns `[[4,1],[5,2],[6,3]]`\n- `rotateRight([[7]])` returns `[[7]]`",
